# korg's runtime environment — the template for /datastore/korg/korg.env on
# kubsdb, which docker-compose.yml reads via `env_file:`.
#
# The real file is NOT in this repo and must never be: deploy/korg.env is
# gitignored. Write it with deploy/cold-start.sh, which takes the password on
# stdin so it never reaches argv, the environment, or shell history.
#
# Only these two keys belong here. KORG_WEB_DIR and KORG_LISTEN_ADDR come from
# the image (Dockerfile ENV); setting them here would just create a second place
# for them to drift, and KORG_FRAME_ANCESTORS (the embed allowlist, #1468) is in
# docker-compose.yml because it is not a secret and belongs somewhere reviewable
# — a gitignored file is the wrong home for "which origins may frame korg".

# Postgres connection for the NON-superuser role `korg`, against the
# `postgresql` container on the shared kubsdb-net network. korg does not use the
# postgres superuser account — that account is the backup and restore path only.
#
# The recoverable copy of this password is k-homelab's age store:
#
#     bin/secret get kubsdb-korg-db-password
#
# Pipe it, never echo it. See docs/operations.md § Cold start.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://korg:REPLACE_ME@postgresql:5432/korg

# Required. korg-core rejects a missing or invalid IANA zone at startup by
# design — no geographic default is guessed — so a first deploy onto a host
# without it crash-loops immediately.
KORG_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles
